  "final": "Done. The cause was in `inventory/stock.py:10`. `reorder_qty` used floor division (`need // pack_size`), so it rounded down to whole packs and ordered less than the need. The huge output came from one test, `test_reorder_rounds_up_to_whole_pack`, which failed 183 times, once per subTest value of `need`.\n\nI changed it to ceiling division, `-(-need // pack_size)`. `python3 -m unittest` now passes: 7 tests, exit 0.\n\nI didn't add a regression test. The existing test already covers this case.",
